course: dictionary
lesson: 9168
title: A snowstorm is a storm of falling snow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snowstorm is a storm with a lot of falling snow, often with strong wind. Look at the two parts: snow is the white flakes that fall from the sky, and storm is rough weather. Put them together and you get a storm full of snow.
explain: The words around a word give clues. In «a heavy snowstorm», the word heavy tells you there is a lot of snow. Snowstorms often make a journey hard, so a story might say someone is «caught in a snowstorm», which means stuck in the middle of one.
explain: Read this from a speaker in Britain or Ireland: «Bit nippy out, innit» in a howling snowstorm. Howling tells you the wind is strong and loud, and nippy means chilly. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence? A snowstorm fits, because a storm with snow and wind is a cold, hard time to be outside.
fact: A snowstorm is a storm with a lot of falling snow, often with strong wind.
fact: In a snowstorm it is hard to see and hard to travel, so stay inside, dress warmly and keep off the roads.
fact: «A heavy snowstorm» means a lot of snow falling fast.
fact: «Caught in a snowstorm» means stuck in the middle of one.
fact: «Like an underwater snowstorm» means many tiny things drifting down together, like snow falling from the sky.
exercise: «The children watched the snowstorm from the window.» What is a snowstorm? | A sunny day at the beach | *A storm with a lot of falling snow and strong wind | A small puddle of rain | A type of cake
exercise: Ahmed reads, «A snowstorm warning was on the radio, so Dad said to stay inside.» Why should you stay inside? | The snowstorm is a party | *The snow makes it hard to see and travel | Dad wants to sleep | Snow is warm and soft
exercise: «It was a heavy snowstorm.» In this sentence, which word tells you there was a lot of snow? | a | winter | *heavy | the
test: «It was a heavy snowstorm, so the school closed.» What does the school closing suggest? | Everyone had a day off for cake | The snow was a surprise party | The school ran out of chairs | *It was too dangerous to travel
test: Which is true about a snowstorm? | It is a kind of pet | It only happens in summer | *It is often windy and hard to see through | It is always hot and dry
exam: Sam says a snowstorm is a light dusting of snow on the grass. Which best explains the word? | A light dusting of snow on the grass | A warm sunny breeze | A puddle left after rain | *A storm with a lot of falling snow, often with strong wind
